== 8. Resting in Performances

#strong[The eighth #emph[device] that Satan has to keep souls from religious services, from holy performances, is,]

By leading them to rest in their performances: to rest in prayer, and to rest in hearing, reading and the communion#footnote[Isa 58:1, 2, 3. Zech 7:4, 5, 6. Matt 6:2. Rom 2:17.] of saints, etc. And when Satan has drawn the soul to rest on the service done, then he will help the soul to reason like this: “Why, you might as well never pray as pray and rest in prayer; as well never hear as hear and rest in hearing; as well never be in the communion of saints as be in it and rest in the communion of saints.” By this device he stops many souls in their heavenly race, and draws poor souls away from the services that should be their joy and crown.

#strong[Now the remedies against this device of Satan are as follows.]

The first #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to dwell much on the imperfections and weaknesses that#footnote[“Pride and high confidence are most apt to creep in upon duties well done,” says one.] attend your#super[+] choicest services. Oh, the spots, the blots, the blemishes that are to be seen on the face of our fairest duties! When you have done all you can, you need to close it all with this: “Do not bring Your servant into judgment, O #smallcaps[Lord], because of the weaknesses that cling to my best services.” We may all#footnote[Isa 64:6.] say with the church, “All our righteous acts are like filthy rags.” If God were strict to mark what is done amiss in our best actions, we would be undone. Oh, the water that is mingled with our wine, the dross that clings to our gold!

The second #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to consider the powerlessness and inability of any of your#super[+] best services to comfort, refresh and bear up your#super[+] souls divinely from fainting and sinking in days of trouble, when darkness is all around you#super[+], when God says to you#super[+], as he once did#footnote[Judg 10:14.] to the Israelites, “Go and cry out to the gods you#super[+] have chosen. Let them save you#super[+] in your#super[+] time of trouble.” So when God says in the day of your#super[+] troubles, “Go to your#super[+] prayers, to your#super[+] hearing and to your#super[+] fasting, etc., and see if they can help you#super[+], if they can support you#super[+], if they can deliver you#super[+]”: if God in that day only withholds the influence of his grace from you, your former services will be but poor heart-medicines to comfort you. And then you must and will cry out, “Oh, none but Christ, none#footnote[#emph[Omne bonum in summo bono]: all good is in the chief good. #emph[Nec Christus nec coelum patitur hyperbolen] \[Neither Christ nor heaven can be overpraised\].] but Christ! Oh, my prayers are not Christ, my hearing is not Christ, my fasting is not Christ, etc.” Oh, one smile of Christ, one glimpse of Christ, one good word from Christ, one nod of love from Christ in the day of trouble and darkness will revive and refresh the soul more than all your#super[+] former services, in which your#super[+] souls rested as if they were the bosom of Christ, which should be the only center of our souls. Christ is the crown of crowns, the glory of glories, and the heaven of heaven.

The third #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is solemnly to consider that good things rested on will as surely undo us and everlastingly destroy us as the greatest enormities we can commit. Those souls who, after they have done all, do not look up as high as Christ, and rest and center in Christ alone, laying down their services at the footstool of Christ, must lie down in sorrow; their bed is prepared for them in hell. “Behold, all#footnote[Isa 50:11.] you#super[+] who kindle a fire, who array yourselves#super[+] with firebrands, walk in the light of your#super[+] fire and of the firebrands you#super[+] have lit! This is what you#super[+] will receive from My hand: You#super[+] will lie down in sorrow.” Is it good to dwell with everlasting burnings, with a devouring fire? If it is, then go on resting in your#super[+] duties; if not, then see that you#super[+] center only in the bosom of Christ.

The fourth and last #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to dwell much on the necessity and excellence of that resting place which God has provided for you#super[+] above all other resting places. He himself is your#super[+] resting place; his free mercy and love is your#super[+] resting place; the pure, glorious, matchless and spotless righteousness of Christ is your#super[+] resting place. Ah, it is sad to think that most men have forgotten their resting place, as the Lord complains: “My people are lost sheep; their shepherds have led them#footnote[Jer 50:6.] astray, causing them to roam the mountains. They have wandered from mountain to hill; they have forgotten their resting place.” So poor souls who do not see the excellence of the resting place that God has appointed for their souls to lie down in wander from mountain to hill, from one duty to another; here they will rest, and there they will rest. But souls who see the excellence of the resting place that God has provided for them will say, “Farewell prayer, farewell hearing, farewell fasting, etc. I will rest no more in you#super[+], but now will rest only in the bosom of Christ, the love of Christ, the righteousness of Christ.”
